                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Where the group lands. The left block walks the ten actual months, the right block the full year: actual to October solid, the rest of the year hatched, against the full-year plan. The forecast comes from the same engine as the actual, so the outlook is not a straight-line extrapolation. A detail for the model builders: the full-year figure is a scalar that sits identically on every month row, so its measure has to take MAX per company and year — SUM would be twelve times too large, and a plain MAX across nine companies would return the largest single one instead of the sum.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "10pt",
                      "color": "#5F6368"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
